A Gift for the Harvest
[trigger road]

FIXME(mundane): A farm girl (~13-14) blocks the road at the edge of a ripe wheat field, arms folded, feet planted wide. She won't let the PC pass unless they help.
FIXME(mundane): The wheat stands tall and golden at her back. Her grandfather works alone at the far edge near a listing wooden fence, reaping with a hand sickle. His back is failing; he pauses between cuts to straighten.
FIXME(strain): Three hired hands didn't show — left for better-paid dock work in Aldgate. The rains come tomorrow. Wet wheat rots; they don't eat this winter.
FIXME(strain): The girl steps close and the desperation she's holding under the bravado shows. Voice cracks once. She swallows.
FIXME(warmth): She offers the PC her grandfather's dinner — fresh bread and cheese her grandmother made — as the only thing she has to trade.
FIXME(mundane): She clocks the PC's guild signet ring and decides guild folk have coin, or time, or something to spare.
